  "final_report": "[stop_reason: hop_cap_reached | hops used: 4/4]\n\nAnalyst summary:\n**Investigation\u202fsummary \u2013 disruption at Aneka Tambang\u202f(TBK) reported\u202f\u2248\u202f30\u202fAug\u202f2019**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Companies that are structurally \u201cat\u2011risk\u201d\n\nThe **down\u2011stream supply\u2011graph (tier\u202f\u2264\u202f2)** from the disrupted firm returned a long list of downstream customers and alternative suppliers.  \nOnly the highest\u2011confidence tier\u20111 names are reproduced in full; the remainder of the tier\u20112 set is listed by sector for context.\n\n| Tier | Company (country) \u2013 primary product / role | Confidence |\n|------|--------------------------------------------|------------|\n| **Tier\u202f1** | **Waskita Karya Persero\u202f(TBK)** \u2013 engineering & construction, precast concrete | medium |\n|  | **POSCO** \u2013 crude and flat\u2011rolled steel (South\u202fKorea) | **high** |\n|  | **SEAH** \u2013 steel pipes & tubes (South\u202fKorea) | **high** |\n|  | **Perusahaan Listrik Negara (PLN)** \u2013 grid electricity transmission/distribution (Indonesia) | **high** |\n|  | **Mitsui** \u2013 steel & metals trading (Japan) | medium |\n|  | **Krakatau Steel Persero\u202f(TBK)** \u2013 hot\u2011rolled / cold\u2011rolled coil (Indonesia) | **high** |\n|  | **SeAH Besteel** \u2013 special/alloy steel & heavy forgings (South\u202fKorea) | **high** |\n|  | **Glencore** \u2013 cobalt (mined, copper by\u2011product) (UK) | **high** |\n| **Tier\u202f2** (selected groups) | Automotive OEMs and parts makers \u2013 e.g., **Stellantis**, **Toyota**, **Hyundai Motor**, **Kia**, **General Motors**, **Tesla** (global) | high |\n|  | Steel\u2011tube / pipe producers \u2013 e.g., **Maruichi Steel Tube**, **Steel Pipe Industry of Indonesia**, **Tenaris** | high |\n|  | Battery\u2011material & cell makers \u2013 e.g., **POSCO Future\u202fM**, **LG Chem**, **Samsung SDI**, **LG Energy Solution**, **SK Innovation**, **Electra Battery Materials**, **Umicore** | high |\n|  | Electric\u2011utility and power\u2011generation firms \u2013 e.g., **AES Corp**, **Korea Electric Power**, **HD Korea Shipbuilding & Offshore Engineering** (as a downstream equipment supplier) | medium\u2011high |\n|  | Miscellaneous downstream users of copper, cobalt or steel \u2013 e.g., **Glencore**, **Alcoa**, **ArcelorMittal**, **Bayerische Motoren Werke**, **Apple**, **Samsung Electronics**, **Schaeffler** | medium\u2011high |\n\n*The full tier\u20112 list (\u2248\u202f150\u202fcompanies) is available in the raw traversal output; it includes many automotive, steel\u2011processing, battery\u2011cell and power\u2011equipment firms that source copper or cobalt downstream of Aneka Tambang.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Evidence collected\n\n| Company | Tool(s) used | What was found |\n|---------|--------------|----------------|\n| **POSCO** | `get_supplier_info` (20\u2011F filing dated\u202f30\u202fApr\u202f2019) \u2013\u202fpre\u2011event; <br>`search_corpus` (query \u201cAneka Tambang\u201d filtered to POSCO, 5\u202ftop results) | The 20\u2011F contains a **mention of Aneka Tambang** in the context of related\u2011party transactions / joint\u2011venture disclosures (the excerpt shows a table of subsidiaries and associated entities where \u201cAneka Tambang\u201d appears). This confirms that POSCO had at least one material relationship with the Indonesian miner before the disruption, making it a plausible downstream user of AT\u2019s copper or cobalt. |\n| **Glencore** | `get_supplier_info` (attempt) | No filing on record for Glencore in the database; therefore no direct documentary evidence could be retrieved. |\n| All other Tier\u20111 and Tier\u20112 companies | \u2013 | No targeted filings or corpus mentions were obtained within the remaining tool budget. Consequently, we cannot confirm whether they have explicit contracts, purchases, or exposure to Aneka Tambang\u2019s output. |\n\n*Note:* The traversal itself is a **structural inference** (based on known supply\u2011chain links) and does not constitute documentary proof of current business with AT. Only POSCO has been corroborated by an actual filing that references AT.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Gaps \u2013 what could NOT be confirmed\n\n| Company / Group | Reason for missing evidence |\n|------------------|------------------------------|\n| **Glencore** (and any other Tier\u20111 firms not covered by a filing) | No SEC/6\u2011K filing exists in the searchable repository; therefore no self\u2011disclosed information is available. |\n| **All Tier\u202f2 companies** (automotive OEMs, battery makers, steel\u2011tube producers, utilities, etc.) | The investigation exhausted the allowed tool calls. No individual filings or corpus hits were retrieved for these entities, so their actual exposure to AT remains *unverified*. |\n| **Any downstream customers that may have informal or private contracts with AT** (e.g., smaller Indonesian fabricators) | Not represented in the public filing set; no evidence could be gathered. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Overall assessment\n\n* The supply\u2011graph shows a **broad network of downstream users**, especially in steel, automotive, battery\u2011materials and electricity generation sectors.  \n* **POSCO** is the only company for which we have concrete documentary proof (a filing that mentions Aneka Tambang) indicating a pre\u2011existing relationship; it should be regarded as the most immediately at\u2011risk downstream partner.  \n* For the remaining high\u2011confidence Tier\u202f1 names (**SEAH, PLN, Krakatau Steel, Mitsui**) and the extensive Tier\u202f2 set, **no public filing or corpus evidence was obtained** within the limited tool budget, so their exposure cannot be confirmed at this stage.  \n\n**Implication:** Stakeholders should prioritize direct outreach to POSCO for clarification of any copper/cobalt supply contracts that may have been disrupted. For all other identified firms, further research (e.g., targeted company\u2011level filings, news searches, or direct supplier questionnaires) will be required to determine the actual impact of the Aneka Tambang disruption.\n\nCOVERAGE GAPS (99) -- reported explicitly, not omitted:\n  - waskita karya persero tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - seah: no evidence gathered\n  - perusahaan perseroan persero pt perusahaan listrik negara: no evidence gathered\n  - mitsui: no evidence gathered\n  - krakatau steel persero tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - seah besteel: no evidence gathered\n  - glencore: no evidence gathered\n  - sjm: no evidence gathered\n  - kg dongbusteel: no evidence gathered\n  - pusan cast iron: no evidence gathered\n  - yeong hwa metal: no evidence gathered\n  - gestamp automocion: no evidence gathered\n  - electra battery materials: no evidence gathered\n  - aes corp/the: no evidence gathered\n  - posco future m: no evidence gathered\n  - eurogroup laminations: no evidence gathered\n  - s-oil: no evidence gathered\n  - kumho petrochemical: no evidence gathered\n  - samsung sdi: no evidence gathered\n  - lg chem: no evidence gathered\n  - apple: no evidence gathered\n  - stellantis: no evidence gathered\n  - toyota motor: no evidence gathered\n  - kg mobility: no evidence gathered\n  - xiamen tungsten: no evidence gathered\n  - sk innovation: no evidence gathered\n  - maruichi steel tube: no evidence gathered\n  - hyundai mobis: no evidence gathered\n  - dongwon metal: no evidence gathered\n  - pp persero tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - wooshin systems: no evidence gathered\n  - cngr advanced material: no evidence gathered\n  - toyoda gosei: no evidence gathered\n  - qst international: no evidence gathered\n  - zhejiang huayou cobalt: no evidence gathered\n  - contemporary amperex technology: no evidence gathered\n  - gm korea: no evidence gathered\n  - samsung electronics: no evidence gathered\n  - gunung raja paksi tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - lg energy solution: no evidence gathered\n  - cia siderurgica 